    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite is green (the `AcceptanceTest` with both cases: default-to-today and keep-supplied-date).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented owner registration date so that when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf: [OwnerFields, \u2026]`, this generates a `LocalDate registrationDate` on both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response), and MapStruct maps it automatically by name. `LocalDate` serializes to ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added the persisted `registration_date` column (`LocalDate`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request to the entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the request omitted it (a supplied date is preserved).\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (tests run on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is required; the `data.sql` seed inserts use named columns so they were unaffected).\n\nThe endpoint wiring already routed create requests through `ValidateOwnerFields \u2192 BuildOwner`, and reads through `RespondWithOwner`, so no YAML/function-pipeline changes were needed \u2014 only the default-fill step and the DTO/entity/schema plumbing.",
